# Reference Caddy config for Wombill.
#
# Wombill v4 runs as a single container on one port: put Caddy in front for
# HTTPS and proxy everything (UI and /api) to that port. No separate API
# upstream, no header juggling — the container's built-in Next proxy forwards
# /api to the backend, and Caddy appends the real client IP so the app's
# TRUST_PROXY=true keeps rate limiting accurate.
#
# - Optional: `tls internal` for LAN-only use (self-signed certs; no ACME).
# - Point this at the port published by docker-compose.prod.yml
#   (127.0.0.1:3010). If Caddy runs in the same compose network, use the
#   service name instead (reverse_proxy app:3010) and drop the host port.

app.example.com {
	encode gzip
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:3010
}

# LAN-only example (self-signed certificate):
# wombill.local {
# 	tls internal
# 	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:3010
# }
